<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="tour-detail-layout">
  <div class="tour-detail-main reveal">
    <h2>Tour Overview</h2>
    <p>Xinjiang is vast —larger than France and Germany combined. This 18-day grand tour does it justice, combining the classic Silk Road route with the breathtaking landscapes of Northern Xinjiang. From the turquoise waters of Kanas Lake in autumn to the rainbow mountains of Zhangye, from the grasslands of Ili to the Sunday Bazaar in Kashgar —this is Xinjiang at its most magnificent.</p>

    <div class="highlight-box"><h3>Trip Highlights</h3><ul>
      <li>Photograph Kanas Lake in golden autumn colors</li><li>Explore Hemu Village, China's most beautiful village</li>
      <li>Trek the Tianshan Mountains near Sayram Lake</li>
      <li>Visit Naraty Grasslands —Kazakh nomad country</li>
      <li>Walk the Mogao Caves in Dunhuang</li>
      <li>Explore the Turpan Depression, 154m below sea level</li>
      <li>Experience Kashgar's legendary Sunday Bazaar</li>
      <li>Camel ride at Singing Sand Dunes</li>
    </ul></div>

    <h2>Day-by-Day Itinerary</h2>
    <ul class="itinerary">
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>1</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Arrive in Urumqi</h4><p>Welcome to Xinjiang's capital. Airport transfer, hotel check-in. Evening visit to Hongshan Park for city views, followed by Uyghur welcome dinner.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Urumqi 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>2</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Urumqi &#9992; Kanas</h4><p>Morning flight to Kanas Airport. Transfer to Kanas Lake Nature Reserve —one of China's most beautiful alpine lakes. Afternoon hike along the lake trail, photographing the famous "Moon Bay" and "Dragon Bay."</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Jiadengyu 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>3</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kanas —Hemu Village</h4><p>Drive to Hemu Village, a remote Tuwa settlement tucked in a valley of birch forests. Horse trek to Beauty Peak for panoramic views. Stay in a cozy wooden lodge.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Hemu Lodge</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>4</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Hemu &#8594; Altay &#8594; Urumqi</h4><p>Sunrise photography at Hemu —the morning mist rising over wooden cabins is iconic. Drive to Altay, visit the Altay Museum, afternoon flight back to Urumqi.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Urumqi 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>5</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Urumqi &#8594; Sayram Lake</h4><p>Morning departure to Sayram Lake (6 hrs). This high-altitude lake is the largest in the Tianshan range, known as the "Last Teardrop of the Atlantic." Afternoon hike around the lake.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Sayram Lake Resort</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>6</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Sayram &#8594; Naraty Grasslands</h4><p>Cross the spectacular Guozigou Bridge en route to Naraty. Spend the afternoon on horseback across the vast alpine grasslands, visiting Kazakh yurt camps.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Naraty Lodge</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>7</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Naraty &#8594; Ili River Valley</h4><p>Drive through the Ili River Valley. Visit lavender fields (Jun-Jul) and local Uyghur villages. Evening arrival in Yining for dinner and rest.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Yining 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>8</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Yining &#9992; Urumqi &#8594; Turpan</h4><p>Morning flight to Urumqi, then drive to Turpan (3 hrs). Visit the ancient Jiaohe Ruins —a Silk Road city carved from raw earth. Evening grape harvest experience at Grape Valley.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Turpan 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>9</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Turpan —Flaming Mountains & Karez</h4><p>Visit the Flaming Mountains, made famous in Journey to the West. Tour the ingenious Karez underground irrigation system. Afternoon at the Emin Minaret and local bazaar.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Turpan 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>10</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Turpan &#8594; Dunhuang (High-speed train)</h4><p>High-speed train to Dunhuang (4 hrs). Evening at Shazhou Night Market for local snacks —try donkey meat noodles and apricot tea.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Dunhuang 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>11</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang —Mogao Caves</h4><p>Full morning at the UNESCO Mogao Caves —492 cave temples with 45,000 sqm of Buddhist murals. Afternoon camel ride at Singing Sand Dunes and sunset at Crescent Moon Spring.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Dunhuang 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>12</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang —Yumen Pass & Yardang Ghost City</h4><p>Drive to Yumen Pass, the ancient frontier gate of the Han Dynasty. Continue to Yardang Ghost City —surreal wind-carved formations in the Gobi Desert.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Dunhuang 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>13</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang &#8594; Jiayuguan &#8594; Zhangye</h4><p>Drive to Jiayuguan (5 hrs). Visit the Jiayuguan Fortress at the western end of the Ming Great Wall. Continue to Zhangye for overnight.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Zhangye 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>14</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Zhangye —Danxia Rainbow Mountains</h4><p>Morning at the Giant Buddha Temple. Afternoon at Zhangye Danxia National Geopark —the multicolored rock formations are at their most vivid in the late afternoon sun.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Zhangye 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>15</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Zhangye &#9992; Kashgar</h4><p>Flight to Kashgar via Urumqi. Afternoon exploring Kashgar Old City's maze of alleyways. Evening tea at a 100-year-old teahouse with live Uyghur music.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Kashgar 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>16</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar —Sunday Bazaar & Karakoram Highway</h4><p>Sunday Market —the ultimate Silk Road experience. Thousands of traders, livestock, spices, and carpets. Afternoon drive along the Karakoram Highway to Karakul Lake.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Kashgar 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>17</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar —Id Kah Mosque & Abakh Khoja Tomb</h4><p>Visit Id Kah Mosque, China's largest. Tour Abakh Khoja Tomb —the "Fragrant Concubine's" mausoleum. Farewell dinner with Uyghur dance performance.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Kashgar 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>18</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Depart Kashgar</h4><p>Airport transfer for departure. Your grand Xinjiang odyssey concludes. &#20877;&#35265;!</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127860; B</span></div></div></li>
    </ul>

